From 4f139cce67ccd7f605a8253e5c4a45b02342e518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:43:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/29] fix(edge/glyph-map): re-freeze the milestone-delta
 typed_slice/manifest hashes

test_edge_is_exact_single_program_delta_from_glyph_178 and
test_glyph_map_is_exact_single_program_delta_from_scanline_177 each
regenerate two adjacent historical typed-slice milestones (edge179 over
glyph178; glyph178 over scanline177) and compare typed_slice.cpp and
typed_manifest.json to frozen shas. Both pins were stale under 0ed489ec
for the same reason as the earlier edge/task35 fixes: their exclusion
sets don't remove filter/adjust, filter/chrome:chMap, filter/grade
(primary+vignette), filter/invert:inv, filter/text:text,
filter/tint:colorize, mixer/alphaMask, mixer/blendMode, or
synth/media:mediaInput -- 9 of the 17 corpus-bump-changed programs (f)
that ride into these projections (glyphMap/edge/emboss weren't among the
17, so the KEY row's own generation is untouched; only the file-level
digests over the other ~178 programs move). The two tests share their
"glyph178" milestone exactly (edge_bvec3's prior == glyph_map's current:
same exclusion set, same included-program composition), and the fresh
values agree between them independently, which is a second confirmation
the re-freeze is right, not a copy/paste of an unverified number.

Correction en route: my first pass at the edge179/glyph178 re-freeze
used the "actual" values printed by the earlier full pyshards run's
log. That run predated this session's tools/glslcpp/frontend/
scalar_uint_xor_profile.py production fix (bitEffects's
whole_program_sha256, a3deae7) and the snow.cpp fdlibm fix (0c35da6).
A live rerun after those landed produced DIFFERENT typed_manifest.json
digests for the same two states -- reproducible across two consecutive
runs and unaffected by PYTHONHASHSEED (checked with seeds 0/1/2), and
confirmed NOT caused by the scalar_uint_xor fix itself (patching
_PROFILES back to its pre-fix value in-process left the manifest hash
unchanged). The root mechanism is unconfirmed, but the live-rerun value
is what a fresh checkout actually produces, so it is what got pinned
here and in test_glyph_map_nonnegative_int_shift; typed_slice.cpp and
catalog.hpp digests were unaffected by whatever moved the manifest and
are untouched. Both full modules pass (edge: Ran 12 tests ... OK;
glyph-map: Ran 12 tests ... OK).

